{
  "rationale": "Plant G1 models the robot's motion and perception interface, exposing all controllable actions and uncontrollable sensor events. The specification E1 encodes the conservative exploration policy: in clear/search states, random_walk is preferred for coverage; after a short forward_commit, the robot returns to clear. Obstacle events force entry to dedicated recovery states, which only allow a single safe turn or, in the worst case, a full_rotate. Recovery states are one-shot and return to clear/search after action or when the path is clear. All uncontrollables are total in every state. The policy avoids unsafe oscillations, disables forward/random_walk in obstacle states, and ensures the robot always recovers before resuming exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant (G1) for all motion and perception events; all events are enabled in all states.",
    "Specification (E1) encodes the exploration and recovery logic: random_walk in clear, move_forward in forward_commit, deterministic turn recovery after obstacles, and full_rotate only as last resort."
